      "title": "Populism poses serious challenge to independent central banks, Bailey says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/04/populism-serious-challenge-independence-central-banks-andrew-bailey",
      "description": "<p>Bank of England governor says central bankers must explain decisions or risk being seen as ‘unrepresentative elite’</p><p>The governor of the Bank of England has said the rise of populist politicians presents a serious challenge to independent central banks.</p><p>As Nigel Farage’s Reform UK <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/brexit-party\">gathered for its annual conference</a> in Birmingham, Andrew Bailey said central bankers must be prepared to explain their decisions to the public or risk being attacked as an “unrepresentative elite”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/04/populism-serious-challenge-independence-central-banks-andrew-bailey\">Continue reading...</a>",
